Hau L. Lee, V. Padmanabhan and Seungjin Whang. Information Distortion in a Supply Chain: The Bullwhip Effect, Management Science 43(4), 546–558, 1997, DOI 10.1287/mnsc.43.4.546. [Publisher](https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/mnsc.43.4.546) · [Author's institutional record](https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/faculty-research/publications/information-distortion-supply-chain-bullwhip-effect).

For advanced information/coordination study obtain the complete article through authorized access, derive its mechanisms and check subsequent comment/correction literature. Test a claim about orders and actual consumption against an explicit chemical replenishment model; an observed variance ratio alone does not identify its cause.

The publisher and author record establish identity, date and abstract scope; paid full text was not inspected on 29 October 2026. Copyright is INFORMS 1997 and open reproduction is not presumed. The complete open inventory book and public courses supply alternatives for foundational work. This reference and its later scholarly responses remain external.

